    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01Xb5LqaNLG6saSgoKaUBss1?thread=cmsg_01Xb5LqaNLG6saSgoKaUBss1JG5WS2CLneVnRb5S9eMFEo)_\n\n## What\n\n- `.config/beets/beets.org`: starter literate config. It tangles two files into `.config/beets/synology/`:\n  - `config.yaml`: beets config (library `/config/musiclibrary.blb`, music `/music`, plugins web, chroma, fetchart, embedart, lastgenre, scrub, info, missing, duplicates). It pulls in `secrets.yaml` with `include:`.\n  - `compose.yaml`: Container Manager project for `lscr.io/linuxserver/beets:latest`, with volumes `/volume1/docker/beets:/config`, `/volume1/music:/music` and `/volume1/music/_import:/downloads`, on port 8337.\n- `.config/beets/deploy-to-synology.sh`: tangles with `emacs -Q --batch` when a tangled file is missing or older than `beets.org` (or when given `-f`), then copies with `scp -O`. Settings come from `-H/-u/-p/-d` or `SYNOLOGY_HOST/USER/PORT/DEST`, with defaults `192.168.88.10`, `$USER`, `22` and `/volume1/docker/beets`. `-n` is a dry run. It copies a local `secrets.yaml` if there is one, and otherwise creates an empty one on the NAS.\n- `.config/beets/.gitignore` keeps `secrets.yaml` and local beets state out of the repo.\n- `README.org`: new **Homelab configuration** section that links to `beets.org` and the script.\n\n## Choices to check\n\n- The files go into `synology/` and not into `~/.config/beets/config.yaml`. That is where a beets on the laptop would look for its config, and the container paths (`/music`, `/config`) would break it.\n- The `web` plugin has to stay enabled, because the image runs `beet web` as its main process and its health check waits for port 8337.\n- `PUID=1026`, `PGID=100`, `TZ=Etc/UTC` and the `/downloads` folder are guesses, marked as such in `beets.org`.\n- I didn't add a CHANGELOG entry, because `CHANGELOG.org` covers only the Emacs config.\n\n## Tested (in a Linux container, not against a real NAS)\n\n- Tangling with Emacs `-Q --batch` writes 6 blocks, and both YAML files parse.\n- The tangled `config.yaml` (with local paths) loads in beets 2.14.1 and `beet ls` works. With `secrets.yaml` missing, beets prints a warning and carries on.\n- The script passes `shellcheck`. I ran it end to end against stub `ssh`/`scp` that write to a local folder: first run tangles, second run skips the tangle, a newer `beets.org` makes it tangle again, `secrets.yaml` gets copied when it exists, and bad port, relative destination, extra arguments and a missing Emacs each fail with a clear message.\n- Not run: real `scp` to DSM, or the container itself.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiBQsat7jnapU9Ud3ka)_",
